# ==============================================================================
# OpenSciencePipe Environment Configuration Template
# ==============================================================================
# Copy this file to .env in the repository root:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Alternatively, run the interactive onboarding wizard:
#   python scripts/setup_keys.py
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TWO SUPPORTED CREDENTIAL WORKFLOWS
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Workflow 1 (standard): this file
#   cp .env.example .env && edit .env
#   Keys are read from the repository root .env file.
#
# Workflow 2 (secure / password manager): cloud-unlock
#   Export the variables below in your shell (e.g., fish):
#       set -gx SCOPUS_API_KEY "your_key"
#   A cloud-unlock helper writes them to a RAM-disk (tmpfs) file at:
#       /run/user/1000/credentials/api_keys.env
#   OpenSciencePipe automatically detects and reads this file.
#
# Precedence order:
#   1. Environment variables (directly set in shell)
#   2. .env file (if present in repository root)
#   3. cloud-unlock tmpfs file (last resort)
#
# IMPORTANT: .env is git-ignored. Never commit real credentials to version control.
# ==============================================================================